{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' attest/specs/151/spec.md; sed -n '1,260p' attest/rulings.md 2>/dev/null || true; rg -n \\\"(stop|STOP|error|Error|failed|FAIL|exception|Exception|Traceback|permission|read-only|sandbox|criterion|criteria|commit|dirty|marker|started|recover|doctor)\\\" attest/records/151/build-01.log | tail -n 180; tail -n 100 attest/records/151/build-01.log\"","aggregated_output":"## Problem\n\nAn invocation that begins and does not end leaves nothing. On 2026-09-17 two build attempts of item #148 died between passing their gates and writing their record: the first with its spawning process, the second under a live one; each left a worktree holding an unrecorded executor commit, no record, no stop, and no line anywhere the product owns. `attavo doctor` held on both, because every proof reads records and a dead invocation writes none; the operator screen rendered the row from the last record and so showed a failed attempt as the whole truth while nothing ran; recovery was three hand-written shell blocks. The product has no primitive for \"this invocation began\", so nothing can say \"and it did not end\".\n\nRetires: the by-hand recovery of a dead or hung drive (the worktree removed, the branch reset, the events archived by a person); the screen's in-memory notion of a running drive as the only witness that one runs; silence as an outcome.\n\n## Claims\n\n- bin/attavo\n- schema/records/build.schema.json\n- schema/records/verify.schema.json\n- schema/manifest.schema.json\n- attavo.toml\n- tests/test_doctor.py\n- tests/test_drive.py\n- tests/test_ledger.py\n\n## Criteria\n\n- doctor-fails-on-an-invocation-without-record.sh: on a fixture tenant with a build-01.started marker naming a dead pid on this host and no build-01.json, attavo doctor --json fails proof no-invocation-lacks-record naming build-01, and holds once build-01.json exists\n- recover-writes-a-died-record.sh: on the same fixture, attavo drive --recover 1 writes build-01.json with status failed and stop class died, provenance product, with a log beside it, committed by the driver identity with a clean tree, after which proof five holds\n- died-and-hung-are-stop-classes.sh: both stage schemas' stop enums name died and hung, the manifest schema declares [drive].stall_after_s, and bin/attavo's STOP_CLASSES names both\n# Rulings\n\nWritten by the merge of a proposed amendment only.\n53:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01WVoCP2ENDykJNLt3jVrc6b\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"40\\trecords = \\\"attest/records\\\"\\n41\\trulings = \\\"attest/rulings.md\\\"\\n42\\trejections = \\\"attest/rejections\\\"\\n43\\t\\n44\\t[operators]\\n45\\tapprovers = [\\\"dbean10\\\"]\\n46\\t\\n47\\t[checks]\\n48\\tcommand = \\\"python3 -m pytest tests -q --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_every_gate_rejects --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_one_item_traversed_every_stage --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_commit_lacks_a_record --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_stop_lacks_cause\\\"\\n49\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"f8b72974-a87c-48c1-9863-33c72a212308\",\"uuid\":\"be336f5e-a423-4e9a-ab35-331a14ab9979\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-17T16:12:34.894Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-151/attavo.toml\",\"content\":\"records = \\\"attest/records\\\"\\nrulings = \\\"attest/rulings.md\\\"\\nrejections = \\\"attest/rejections\\\"\\n\\n[operators]\\napprovers = [\\\"dbean10\\\"]\\n\\n[checks]\\ncommand = \\\"python3 -m pytest tests -q --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_every_gate_rejects --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_one_item_traversed_every_stage --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_commit_lacks_a_record --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_stop_lacks_cause\\\"\\n\",\"numLines\":10,\"startLine\":40,\"totalLines\":