es not end leaves nothing. On 2026-09-17 two build attempts of item #148 died between passing their gates and writing their record: the first with its spawning process, the second under a live one; each left a worktree holding an unrecorded executor commit, no record, no stop, and no line anywhere the product owns. `attavo doctor` held on both, because every proof reads records and a dead invocation writes none; the operator screen rendered the row from the last record and so showed a failed attempt as the whole truth while nothing ran; recovery was three hand-written shell blocks. The product has no primitive for \"this invocation began\", so nothing can say \"and it did not end\".\n169:+Retires: the by-hand recovery of a dead or hung drive (the worktree removed, the branch reset, the events archived by a person); the screen's in-memory notion of a running drive as the only witness that one runs; silence as an outcome.\n184:+- doctor-fails-on-an-invocation-without-record.sh: on a fixture tenant with a build-01.started marker naming a dead pid on this host and no build-01.json, attavo doctor --json fails proof no-invocation-lacks-record naming build-01, and holds once build-01.json exists\n185:+- recover-writes-a-died-record.sh: on the same fixture, attavo drive --recover 1 writes build-01.json with status failed and stop class died, provenance product, with a log beside it, committed by the driver identity with a clean tree, after which proof five holds\n186:+- died-and-hung-are-stop-classes.sh: both stage schemas' stop enums name died and hung, the manifest schema declares [drive].stall_after_s, and bin/attavo's STOP_CLASSES names both\n243:+stall_after_s = 1800\n483:+alone raised (GUARDED_STOP_CLASSES), else \"none\". A record too old to\n787:+STOP_CLASSES = (\"non-question\", \"outlived-invocation\", \"no-cause\", \"forge-unconcluded\",\n789:+               \"environment\", \"gate\", \"died\", \"hung\")\n836:+# last line, since cmd_build and cmd_verify both append \"[adapter exited\n862:+    \"\"\"Whichever of STOP_CLASSES this text names -- its own spelling, or\n872:+    for name in STOP_CLASSES:\n886:+        line (issue #88, #94), when it names a STOP_CLASSES member -- is\n938:+    if report_class in STOP_CLASSES:\n1056:+INVOCATION_MARKER_SUFFIX = \".started\"\n1065:+    host, pid, the sha it starts on, and the product that started it.\n1067:+    an invocation that died or hangs, and proof five names it.\"\"\"\n1084:+    that ran elsewhere and wrote no record is died by absence.\"\"\"\n1102:+    \"\"\"Every <stage>-NN.started under one item whose <stage>-NN.json has\n1119:+    \"\"\"[drive].stall_after_s: the tenant's own bound past which a live\n1120:+    invocation with no new event is hung. A bound the tenant did not\n1122:+    bound = (m.get(\"drive\") or {}).get(\"stall_after_s\")\n1129:+    p = Proof(\"no-invocation-lacks-record\", \"no invocation lacks its record\")\n1137:+        return p.fail(\"no [drive].stall_after_s in the manifest; a hung invocation cannot be \"\n1151:+            problems.append(f\"{name} started {info.get('at')} on {info.get('host')} \"\n1205:+def _drive_recover(root: Path, m: dict, item_id: str) -> int:\n1206:+    \"\"\"`attavo drive --recover [N]`: every invocation of item N that began\n1207:+    and wrote no record ends in one here -- class died when its pid is\n1208:+    gone or on another host, class hung when it is alive past\n1209:+    [drive].stall_after_s with no newer event (and terminated); provenance\n1220:+        print(\"attavo drive: refused: no [drive].stall_after_s in the manifest; a hung \"\n1225:+        print(f\"attavo drive: item {item_id}: every invocation has its record; nothing to recover\")\n1233:+    recovered = 0\n1245:+                      f\"nothing to recover\")\n1247:+            cls = \"hung\"\n1256:+            cls = \"died\"\n1258:+                      f\"started {info.get('at')}, last event {last_at or 'none'}\")\n1262:+                  f\"a later record already exists, read the records before recovering\")\n1282:+                                        f\"({path.stem}), recovered as {cls}\")\n1293:+        print(f\"attavo drive: recovered {marker.stem} as {cls}: {detail}\")\n1294:+        recovered += 1\n1295:+    print(f\"attavo drive: item {item_id}: {recovered} invocation(s) recovered\")\n1453:+ADAPTER_EXIT_RE = re.compile(r\"^\\[adapter exited \\d+\\]$\")\n1461:+    \"thread.started\" event, then nothing but \"[adapter exited 1]\" -- the\n1508:+                if cls not in STOP_CLASSES:\n1550:+            if cls not in STOP_CLASSES:\n2046:+# #115). question (a person's to answer) and the residual (no-cause,\n2051:+GUARDED_STOP_CLASSES = (\"non-question\", \"outlived-invocation\", \"forge-unconcluded\", \"ceiling\",\n2057:+    enum (issue #129) rather than retyped -- STOP_CLASSES already drifted\n2200:+    started = time.monotonic()\n2234:+                \"wall_clock_s\": round(time.monotonic() - started, 3),\n2291:+                detail = f\"[adapter exited {run.returncode}]\"\n2428:+        \"wall_clock_s\": round(time.monotonic() - started, 3),\n2543:+    started = time.monotonic()\n2569:+            \"wall_clock_s\": round(time.monotonic() - started, 3),\n2621:+            detail = f\"[adapter exited {run.returncode}]\"\n2677:+        \"wall_clock_s\": round(time.monotonic() - started, 3),\n2769:+    started = time.monotonic()\n2791:+            detail = f\"[adapter exited {run.returncode}]\"\n2831:+        \"wall_clock_s\": round(time.monotonic() - started, 3),\n2996:+        commit_record(root, [marker], f\"attavo: {stage} invocation {nn:02d} started for item {item_id}\")\n3099:+    recover = \"--recover\" in argv\n3100:+    positional = [a for a in argv if a not in (\"--until-ready\", \"--recover\")]\n3112:+    if recover:\n3113:+        return _drive_recover(root, m, item_id)\n3774:+    guard's); failing that, \"guard\" for a class in GUARDED_STOP_CLASSES\n3776:+    -- no-cause, unclassed, or no stop at all -- is \"none\": nobody has\n3796:+        elif stop and stop.get(\"class\") in GUARDED_STOP_CLASSES:\n4151:+alone raised (GUARDED_STOP_CLASSES), else \"none\". A record too old to\n4455:+STOP_CLASSES = (\"non-question\", \"outlived-invocation\", \"no-cause\", \"forge-unconcluded\",\n4504:+# last line, since cmd_build and cmd_verify both append \"[adapter exited\n4530:+    \"\"\"Whichever of STOP_CLASSES this text names -- its own spelling, or\n4540:+    for name in STOP_CLASSES:\n4554:+        line (issue #88, #94), when it names a STOP_CLASSES member -- is\n4606:+    if report_class in STOP_CLASSES:\n4878:+ADAPTER_EXIT_RE = re.compile(r\"^\\[adapter exited \\d+\\]$\")\n4886:+    \"thread.started\" event, then nothing but \"[adapter exited 1]\" -- the\n4933:+                if cls not in STOP_CLASSES:\n4975:+            if cls not in STOP_CLASSES:\n5470:+# #115). question (a person's to answer) and the residual (no-cause,\n5475:+GUARDED_STOP_CLASSES = (\"non-question\", \"outlived-invocation\", \"forge-unconcluded\", \"ceiling\",\n5481:+    enum (issue #129) rather than retyped -- STOP_CLASSES already drifted\n5624:+    started = time.monotonic()\n5658:+                \"wall_clock_s\": round(time.monotonic() - started, 3),\n5715:+                detail = f\"[adapter exited {run.returncode}]\"\n5852:+        \"wall_clock_s\": round(time.monotonic() - started, 3),\n5967:+    started = time.monotonic()\n5993:+            \"wall_clock_s\": round(time.monotonic() - started, 3),\n6045:+            detail = f\"[adapter exited {run.returncode}]\"\n6101:+        \"wall_clock_s\": round(time.monotonic() - started, 3),\n6193:+    started = time.monotonic()\n6215:+            detail = f\"[adapter exited {run.returncode}]\"\n6255:+        \"wall_clock_s\": round(time.monotonic() - started, 3),\n7172:+    guard's); failing that, \"guard\" for a class in GUARDED_STOP_CLASSES\n7174:+    -- no-cause, unclassed, or no stop at all -- is \"none\": nobody has\n7194:+        elif stop and stop.get(\"class\") in GUARDED_STOP_CLASSES:\n7559:+        \"stall_after_s\": {\n7562:+          \"description\": \"seconds without a new event past which a live invocation is hung; attavo drive --recover terminates and records it\"\n7850:+            \"no-cause\",\n7859:+            \"died\",\n7860:+            \"hung\"\n8191:+            \"no-cause\",\n8198:+            \"died\",\n8199:+            \"hung\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '520,735p' /Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo; sed -n '110,155p' /Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo; sed -n '2190,2295p' /Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo; sed -n '1,220p' attest/specs/151/criteria/doctor-fails-on-an-invocation-without-record.sh; sed -n '1,240p' attest/specs/151/criteria/recover-writes-a-died-record.sh; sed -n '1,160p' attest/specs/151/criteria/died-and-hung-are-stop-classes.sh\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '520,735p' /Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo; sed -n '110,155p' /Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo; sed -n '2190,2295p' /Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/bin/attavo; sed -n '1,220p' attest/specs/151/criteria/doctor-fails-on-an-invocation-without-record.sh; sed -n '1,240p' attest/specs/151/criteria/recover-writes-a-died-record.sh; sed -n '1,160p' attest/specs/151/criteria/died-and-hung-are-stop-classes.sh\"","aggregated_output":"    if (record.get(\"status\") == \"failed\" and not log\n            and record.get(\"refusal\") is None and record.get(\"halted\") is None):\n        raise ValueError(f\"write_record: {stage} record status is 'failed' with no log, \"\n                         f\"refusal, or halted to say why\")\n    path = records_dir / f\"{stage}-{nn:02d}.json\"\n    if log is not None:\n        path.with_suffix(\".log\").write_text(log)\n    path.write_text(json.dumps(record, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n    return path\n\n\n# --- stop: every non-pass build or verify record's class and cause (issue\n# #89) -- derived here, at write time, from the refusal, halted, and log\n# the caller already has. Never a fresh read of anything: the tenant zero\n# specimens this retires (#576 build-11, #659 build-01 and verify-01) are\n# exactly a stop the product wrote with nothing beside it to explain\n# itself after the fact. ---\n\nSTOP_CLASSES = (\"non-question\", \"outlived-invocation\", \"no-cause\", \"forge-unconcluded\",\n               \"ceiling\", \"claims-boundary\", \"repeated-act\", \"unclassed\", \"question\",\n               \"environment\", \"gate\")\nSTOP_PROVENANCES = (\"product\", \"tenant\", \"executor\", \"spec\")\n\n# Beyond the enum spelling itself, the prose issue #88 actually shipped\n# (adapters/claude-code/run and adapters/codex/run, on main since\n# v0.16.0) once put a class's own name, or a real specimen's wording of\n# it, in the transcript for the generic match below to find. Issue #94\n# moves non-question and outlived-invocation onto report_class instead\n# (below): non-question's own halt line (\"halted: class non-question\")\n# would otherwise still satisfy the bare-name match here with no adapter\n# report-line field involved at all, and outlived-invocation's refusal\n# never named its class in text to begin with, so both are disabled here\n# -- the same pattern issue #93 established for ceiling, just below,\n# rather than removed outright.\nCLASS_TEXT_MARKERS: dict[str, tuple[str, ...]] = {\n    \"non-question\": (),\n    \"outlived-invocation\": (),\n    # Issue #93: ceiling's own text-based check is CEILING_MARKERS, below,\n    # with provenance \"product\" -- a fact about the tool, not an executor\n    # judgment like non-question/outlived-invocation are. Left at the\n    # default (the class's own name, \"ceiling\"), the generic match above\n    # would instead catch adapters/codex/run's and\n    # adapters/claude-code/run's own pre-emptive refusal -- which must\n    # carry the word \"ceiling\" by the same issue's own brief -- as\n    # provenance \"executor\", before CEILING_MARKERS is ever consulted.\n    \"ceiling\": (),\n    # A genuine question (issue #100's own followups) is read structurally\n    # -- status \"halted\" carrying a non-empty halted.question -- not by\n    # scanning for the literal word \"question\", which the question's own\n    # text very often contains regardless of what it is actually asking.\n    # Left at the default, the generic match above would misclassify any\n    # question that happens to use the word \"question\" as executor\n    # provenance, before the structural check in derive_stop is reached.\n    \"question\": (),\n    # environment/tenant (issue #115) is set directly by cmd_build's own\n    # preflight -- the one caller who knows a [checks].command exited 2\n    # on the approved tree -- never derived from adapter text. Left at\n    # the default, the generic match above would catch the word\n    # \"environment\" anywhere in a log or refusal (e.g. codex's own\n    # OPENAI_API_KEY auth-mismatch refusal, adapters/codex/run's\n    # check_auth) as an environment/executor stop that never happened.\n    \"environment\": (),\n}\n\n# Known tool error text for a declared ceiling -- issue #86's own specimen\n# (codex's \"Input exceeds...\" line on a diff too large to judge) is\n# \"input_too_large\"; a matching line anywhere in the log, not only its\n# last line, since cmd_build and cmd_verify both append \"[adapter exited\n# N]\" after whatever the tool itself printed. \"ceiling exceeded\" is issue\n# #93's own addition: both adapters now refuse pre-emptively, before the\n# tool is ever invoked, against a declared or fixed input limit, and\n# their refusal text is not caught by any of the three markers above.\nCEILING_MARKERS = (\"input_too_large\", \"exceeds the maximum context length\",\n                  \"context_length_exceeded\", \"ceiling exceeded\")\n\n\n# Issue #100's followups: an unclassed detail is the log's last line\n# verbatim, and that line is sometimes an adapter's own event JSON or a\n# tool's full error text -- thousands of characters wide. Capped here,\n# at write time, so a filed issue's own summary of it (file-stops'\n# log_tail already carries the full picture) stays short; the class\n# itself, \"unclassed\", already says the full explanation lives in the\n# log, not in this field.\nUNCLASSED_DETAIL_MAX_CHARS = 200\n\n\ndef _log_last_line(log: str | None) -> str:\n    lines = [l for l in (log or \"\").splitlines() if l.strip()]\n    last = lines[-1] if lines else \"\"\n    return last[:UNCLASSED_DETAIL_MAX_CHARS]\n\n\ndef _carries_a_known_class(text: str | None) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"Whichever of STOP_CLASSES this text names -- its own spelling, or\n    one of CLASS_TEXT_MARKERS' real-world phrasings of it, when that\n    class is not disabled there -- or None. Issue #88 is where an\n    adapter's own halt or refusal first named its class this way; issue\n    #93 added ceiling's own pre-emptive refusal to that set and disabled\n    its bare-name match (CEILING_MARKERS covers it instead); issue #94\n    disables non-question and outlived-invocation the same way, reading\n    both from the adapter's own report line (derive_stop's report_class)\n    now instead.\"\"\"\n    text = text or \"\"\n    for name in STOP_CLASSES:\n        markers = CLASS_TEXT_MARKERS.get(name, (name,))\n        if any(marker in text for marker in markers):\n            return name\n    return None\n\n\ndef derive_stop(status: str, *, refusal: str | None = None, halted: dict | None = None,\n                log: str | None = None, report_class: str | None = None,\n                refusal_provenance: str | None = None) -> dict | None:\n    \"\"\"The stop field for a build or verify record: None for status \"pass\",\n    else {class, provenance, detail} from what the caller already knows.\n\n      - report_class -- payload.get(\"class\") off the adapter's own report\n        line (issue #88, #94), when it names a STOP_CLASSES member -- is\n        that class, provenance \"executor\". build.schema.json and\n        verify.schema.json stay untouched by issue #88 on purpose, so the\n        class lives only on the report line, never a structured field\n        cmd_build or cmd_verify forwards on its own account; the caller\n        reads payload itself and passes this in, since only it still has\n        payload once an iteration ends. This is non-question's and\n        outlived-invocation's only path to a record now (issue #94):\n        CLASS_TEXT_MARKERS disables both for the text scan below, the\n        same way issue #93 disabled ceiling's bare-name match there. A\n        class an adapter does not yet put on its report line --\n        outlived-invocation today, since that refusal path prints no\n        report line at all -- falls to unclassed below, same as any\n        other unnamed cause, until the adapter that raises it puts a\n        class on the line the way non-question already does.\n      - a halt carrying a non-empty halted.question, once it is not a\n        non-question caught above, is a genuine question -- question/spec,\n        with the question's own first line as detail (issue #100's\n        followups). This is the specimen issue #100 itself was built to\n        retire: tenant zero's #663 build-01, a proper question, classed\n        unclassed/product and filed as a product defect with the wrong\n        provenance -- a question is about the definition of done, which is\n        a person's or a ruling's to answer, never the product's own\n        mechanism.\n      - failing that, a refusal or the log itself that already names its\n        class in text (issue #88, #93 for ceiling's own pre-emptive\n        refusal) is that class, provenance \"executor\" -- the log is\n        checked because neither adapter's refusal *field* carries the\n        class today; the class-naming line each adapter prints reaches\n        only the transcript\n      - a refusal that is not that -- the write-outside-claims path\n        itself, not the \"commit ... not authored by the executor\" shape\n        -- is claims-boundary/spec, unless the caller already knows this\n        refusal touched paths.records or paths.specs (issue #140:\n        protected_path_touched, checked ahead of the ordinary claims\n        match in cmd_build) and passes refusal_provenance=\"executor\" --\n        the product's own directories are not a claim a spec makes, so a\n        refusal there is not the spec's boundary to answer for\n      - a returned verify (the forge was not green; no adapter ran) is\n        forge-unconcluded/tenant\n      - an adapter exit whose log carries a declared-ceiling error line is\n        ceiling/product\n      - anything else is unclassed/product, with the log's last line\n        (capped at UNCLASSED_DETAIL_MAX_CHARS) as its detail -- the other\n        class that carries a detail, since every remaining class's\n        evidence already lives in refusal, halted, forge_checks, or the\n        log itself.\n    \"\"\"\n    if status == \"pass\":\n        return None\n    if status == \"returned\":\n        return {\"class\": \"forge-unconcluded\", \"provenance\": \"tenant\", \"detail\": None}\n    if report_class in STOP_CLASSES:\n        return {\"class\": report_class, \"provenance\": \"executor\", \"detail\": None}\n    question = (halted or {}).get(\"question\")\n    if status == \"halted\" and question:\n        return {\"class\": \"question\", \"provenance\": \"spec\",\n               \"detail\": question.splitlines()[0]}\n    known = _carries_a_known_class(refusal) or _carries_a_known_class(log)\n    if known:\n        return {\"class\": known, \"provenance\": \"executor\", \"detail\": None}\n    if status == \"refused\" and refusal is not None and not refusal.startswith(\"commit \"):\n        return {\"class\": \"claims-boundary\", \"provenance\": refusal_provenance or \"spec\",\n               \"detail\": None}\n    if log and any(marker in log.lower() for marker in CEILING_MARKERS):\n        return {\"class\": \"ceiling\", \"provenance\": \"product\", \"detail\": None}\n    return {\"class\": \"unclassed\", \"provenance\": \"product\", \"detail\": _log_last_line(log)}\n\n\ndef gate_stop(refusal: str | None) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"The stop for a refused spec-gate record: class \"gate\", provenance\n    \"spec\", the refusal string itself as cause (issue #137) -- not\n    derive_stop's generic claims-boundary/spec fallback issue #133\n    reused, which named a boundary the record never crossed: \"criterion\n    fails against the tree plus stub: doctor-template-absent.sh\" is not\n    a write outside claims. cmd_spec_gate is untouched by this lane, so\n    a spec record still carries no stop field of its own; this is\n    synthesized wherever a refused one is read (item_stops,\n    cmd_file_stops, proof_no_stop_lacks_cause), never persisted.\"\"\"\n    return {\"class\": \"gate\", \"provenance\": \"spec\", \"detail\": refusal}\n\n\ndef load_records(records_dir: Path) -> dict[str, dict[str, dict]]:\n    \"\"\"{item_id: {stage: latest_record}} for every <records>/<item>/<stage>-NN.json.\"\"\"\n    items: dict[str, dict[str, dict]] = {}\n    if not records_dir.is_dir():\n        return items\n    for item_dir in sorted(p for p in records_dir.iterdir() if p.is_dir()):\n        by_stage: dict[str, dict[int, dict]] = {}\n        for rec in sorted(item_dir.glob(\"*.json\")):\n            m = RECORD_RE.match(rec.name)\n            if not m:\n                continue\n            stage, n = m.group(1), int(m.group(2))\n            try:\n                data = _load_record(rec, item_dir.name)\n            except json.JSONDecodeError:\n                continue\n            by_stage.setdefault(stage, {})[n] = data\n\nfile-stops opens one tenant issue per stop record of the item with no\nissue filed for it yet, through [forge].file_issue_command, naming the\nclass, the provenance, the record path, and the log's last twenty\nlines; a record it has already filed carries a <stage>-NN.filed marker\nbeside it, holding the filing command's own stdout, so a second run\nfiles nothing new. Like a build or verify record, this command writes\nthe marker and leaves it uncommitted -- drive commits it, in the same\ncommit as the record it names (issue #89). It refuses (exit 1,\nnothing filed) a stop whose class is unclassed and whose detail is\nempty -- a stop the product cannot even describe is not filed as if it\ncould. See issue #89's lane for the full rules it enforces.\n\ncounsel reads the item's latest non-pass build or verify record -- or,\nwhen neither exists, its latest refused spec-gate record, the earliest\npoint a question can be answered inside the product, before any\napproval or executor spend (issue #133) -- and asks the tenant's\n[executor].counsel adapter (defaulting to [executor].verify) a\nread-only question about it: the record, its log, the spec (problem,\nclaims, criteria, stub, including stub/.removed), paths.rulings, the\nitem's diff since approval, the tenant manifest, and this product's own\nroot (bin/attavo, adapters/, schema/, templates/) by path, under the\nsame sandbox verify runs under. The adapter answers with class (the\nstop enumeration, or unclassed), verdict (answer: a ruling text with\ncitations; patch: a product defect's file, symbol, rejection test, and\ndiff; person: a one-line question no rule covers), citations\n(instruction, mechanism, guard, each a path and symbol or a ruling id),\nand proposal (the ruling text, the patch, or the question). It writes\nthe next counsel-NN.json under paths.records/N/, with the adapter's\ntranscript beside it as counsel-NN.log, and commits nothing -- the\ncaller commits, as with every stage. It refuses (exit 1, nothing\nwritten) when the item carries no non-pass build, verify, or spec-gate\nrecord to counsel. See issue #100's lane for the full rules it\nenforces, and issue #133's for the spec-gate fallback.\n\nrecord-only exits 0 when HEAD, against its first parent, touches only\npaths.records; 1 otherwise; 2 with no manifest. Core logic about a git\ncheckout, not a forge's shell -- a workflow template's push-and-retrigger\nguard is one line reading this exit code instead of carrying its own\ncopy of the check.\n\nattest refuses (exit 1) unless the latest spec, approval, build, and\nverify records for an item all exist and chain: the build's approval_sha\nnames the latest approval, and the verify's build_sha names that build --\na re-approval after a build must force a re-run of what changed. With no\nN given it derives the item from the record paths HEAD's merge commit\n\n    print(f\"attavo verify: {status_out} ({record_path.name})\")\n    return 0 if status_out == \"pass\" else 1\n\n\n# --- counsel: a stop is read inside the product first, before a person\n# (issue #100). Read-only -- it commits nothing and writes nothing outside\n# paths.records/<N>/ -- and it never acts: it proposes a ruling, a patch,\n# or names the one-line question a person must answer. ---\n\nCOUNSEL_STAGES = (\"build\", \"verify\")\n\n\ndef latest_non_pass_stage_record(records_dir: Path) -> tuple[str | None, dict | None, Path | None]:\n    \"\"\"(stage, record, path) for the item's most recent non-pass build or\n    verify record, by its own \"at\" timestamp -- or, when neither stage\n    carries one, the item's latest refused spec-gate record (issue #133):\n    a refused gate is the same shape of stop, earlier, and it is read only\n    once a build or verify record exists to counsel first, since either\n    one already implies the gate that produced it passed. (None, None,\n    None) when none of the three exists. \"Most recent\" rather than\n    \"build, else verify\" so a stop on the stage that ran later (typically\n    verify, bound to a build that already passed) is the one counseled.\"\"\"\n    candidates: list[tuple[str, dict, Path]] = []\n    for stage in COUNSEL_STAGES:\n        path = latest_attempt_path(records_dir, stage)\n        if path is None:\n            continue\n        rec = latest_record(records_dir, stage)\n        if rec.get(\"status\") == \"pass\":\n            continue\n        candidates.append((stage, rec, path))\n    if candidates:\n        candidates.sort(key=lambda c: c[1].get(\"at\") or \"\")\n        return candidates[-1]\n    spec_path = latest_attempt_path(records_dir, \"spec\")\n    if spec_path is not None:\n        spec_rec = latest_record(records_dir, \"spec\")\n        if spec_rec.get(\"status\") == \"refused\":\n            return \"spec\", spec_rec, spec_path\n    return None, None, None\n\n\ndef cmd_counsel(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n    root = Path(\".\").resolve()\n    item_id = argv[0] if argv else derive_item_id(root)\n    if not item_id:\n        print(\"attavo counsel: cannot derive item id; pass N or run on an attavo/N-* branch\",\n              file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    m = read_manifest(root)\n    if m is None:\n        print(f\"attavo counsel: no {MANIFEST} at {root}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n\n    specs_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"specs\"]\n    records_rel = m[\"paths\"][\"records\"]\n    item_records_dir = root / records_rel / item_id\n\n    stage, stop_record, record_path = latest_non_pass_stage_record(item_records_dir)\n    if stop_record is None:\n        print(f\"attavo counsel: refused: no non-pass build, verify, or spec-gate record \"\n              f\"for item {item_id}\")\n        return 1\n\n    executor = m.get(\"executor\") or {}\n    adapter_name = executor.get(\"counsel\") or executor.get(\"verify\")\n    if not adapter_name:\n        print(\"attavo counsel: refused: no [executor].counsel or [executor].verify \"\n              \"in the manifest\")\n        return 1\n    adapter_path = resolve_adapter(root, adapter_name)\n    if adapter_path is None:\n        print(f\"attavo counsel: refused: no adapter named {adapter_name!r}\")\n        return 1\n\n    adapter_config = merge_adapter_config(m, adapter_name, \"counsel\")\n    reports = adapter_reports(adapter_path)\n    spec_dir = root / specs_rel / item_id\n    log_path = record_path.with_suffix(\".log\")\n\n    diff_text, diff_refusal = diff_since_approval(root, stop_record.get(\"approval_sha\"))\n    if diff_refusal:\n        print(f\"attavo counsel: refused: {diff_refusal}\")\n        return 1\n\n    started = time.monotonic()\n\n    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tmp:\n        diff_path = Path(tmp) / \"diff.patch\"\n        diff_path.write_text(diff_text)\n\n        env = dict(os.environ)\n        env[\"ATTAVO_SPEC_DIR\"] = str(spec_dir)\n        env[\"ATTAVO_RECORDS_DIR\"] = str(item_records_dir)\n        env[\"ATTAVO_RULINGS\"] = str(root / m[\"paths\"][\"rulings\"])\n        env[\"ATTAVO_STAGE\"] = \"counsel\"\n        env[\"ATTAVO_COUNSEL_RECORD\"] = str(record_path)\n        env[\"ATTAVO_COUNSEL_LOG\"] = str(log_path) if log_path.is_file() else \"\"\n        env[\"ATTAVO_COUNSEL_DIFF\"] = str(diff_path)\n        env[\"ATTAVO_MANIFEST\"] = str(root / MANIFEST)\n        env[\"ATTAVO_PRODUCT_ROOT\"] = str(PRODUCT_ROOT)\n        env[\"ATTAVO_ADAPTER_CONFIG\"] = json.dumps(adapter_config)\n\n        run = subprocess.run([str(adapter_path)], cwd=str(root), env=env,\n                             capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n#!/bin/sh\nset -e\nhere=$(pwd)\ntmp=$(mktemp -d)\ncd \"$tmp\"\ngit init -q -b main .\ngit config user.email doctor@attavo.invalid\ngit config user.name \"doctor fixture\"\nprintf '[paths]\\nrecords = \"records\"\\n\\n[drive]\\nstall_after_s = 60\\n' > attavo.toml\ngit add attavo.toml\ngit commit -q -m install\nmkdir -p records/1\nsleep 0 &\ndead=$!\nwait \"$dead\"\npython3 - \"$tmp/records/1/build-01.started\" \"$dead\" <<'PY'\nimport json, socket, sys\njson.dump({\"at\": \"2026-09-17T13:16:08Z\", \"host\": socket.gethostname(), \"pid\": int(sys.argv[2]),\n           \"sha\": \"0000000000000000000000000000000000000000\", \"product_version\": \"fixture\"},\n          open(sys.argv[1], \"w\"))\nPY\ngit add records\ngit commit -q -m \"invocation marker for item 1\"\ncd \"$here\"\npython3 bin/attavo doctor --json \"$tmp\" > \"$tmp/doctor-without.json\" || true\nprintf '{\"status\": \"pass\"}' > \"$tmp/records/1/build-01.json\"\npython3 bin/attavo doctor --json \"$tmp\" > \"$tmp/doctor-with.json\" || true\npython3 - \"$tmp/doctor-without.json\" \"$tmp/doctor-with.json\" <<'PY'\nimport json, sys\ndef proof(path):\n    d = json.load(open(path))\n    return [x for x in d[\"proofs\"] if x[\"proof\"] == \"no-invocation-lacks-record\"][0]\nwithout = proof(sys.argv[1])\nassert without[\"holds\"] is False, without\nassert \"build-01\" in without[\"reason\"] and \"never wrote its record\" in without[\"reason\"], without\nwith_record = proof(sys.argv[2])\nassert with_record[\"holds\"] is True, with_record\nPY\nrm -rf \"$tmp\"\n#!/bin/sh\nset -e\nhere=$(pwd)\ntmp=$(mktemp -d)\ncd \"$tmp\"\ngit init -q -b main .\ngit config user.email person@attavo.invalid\ngit config user.name \"recover fixture\"\nprintf '[paths]\\nrecords = \"records\"\\n\\n[drive]\\nstall_after_s = 60\\n\\n[executor]\\nbuild = \"fixture\"\\n' > attavo.toml\ngit add attavo.toml\ngit commit -q -m install\ngit checkout -q -b attavo/1-x\nmkdir -p records/1\nsleep 0 &\ndead=$!\nwait \"$dead\"\npython3 - \"$tmp/records/1/build-01.started\" \"$dead\" <<'PY'\nimport json, socket, sys\njson.dump({\"at\": \"2026-09-17T13:16:08Z\", \"host\": socket.gethostname(), \"pid\": int(sys.argv[2]),\n           \"sha\": \"0000000000000000000000000000000000000000\", \"product_version\": \"fixture\"},\n          open(sys.argv[1], \"w\"))\nPY\ngit add records\ngit commit -q -m \"invocation marker for item 1\"\npython3 \"$here/bin/attavo\" drive --recover 1\ntest -f records/1/build-01.json\ntest -f records/1/build-01.log\npython3 - records/1/build-01.json <<'PY'\nimport json, sys\nr = json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))\nassert r[\"status\"] == \"failed\", r\nassert r[\"stop\"][\"class\"] == \"died\" and r[\"stop\"][\"provenance\"] == \"product\", r[\"stop\"]\nassert \"wrote no build-01.json\" in r[\"stop\"][\"detail\"], r[\"stop\"]\nPY\ntest \"$(git log -1 --format=%an)\" = \"attavo driver\"\ntest -z \"$(git status --porcelain)\"\ncd \"$here\"\npython3 bin/attavo doctor --json \"$tmp\" | python3 -c 'import json,sys; p=[x for x in json.load(sys.stdin)[\"proofs\"] if x[\"proof\"]==\"no-invocation-lacks-record\"][0]; assert p[\"holds\"] is True, p'\nrm -rf \"$tmp\"\n#!/bin/sh\nset -e\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor stage in (\"build\", \"verify\"):\n    enum = json.load(open(f\"schema/records/{stage}.schema.json\"))[\"properties\"][\"stop\"][\"properties\"][\"class\"][\"enum\"]\n    assert \"died\" in enum and \"hung\" in enum, (stage, enum)\ndrive = json.load(open(\"schema/manifest.schema.json\"))[\"properties\"][\"drive\"]\nassert \"stall_after_s\" in drive[\"properties\"], drive\nPY\ngrep -q '\"died\", \"hung\"' bin/attavo\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
